 "text": "Departments | Neosho County, KS\nLoading\nSkip to Main Content\nCreate a Website Account - Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.\nWebsite Sign In\nSearch\nGovernment\nDepartments\nServices\nCommunity\nBusiness\nHow Do I...\nHighway Project\nAgendas & Minutes\nEmployment\nTaxes\nWatch Meetings\nNotify Me®\nEmergency Notifications\nHome\nDepartments\nDepartments\n9\n1\n1\n2\n911 Communications\nAccess more information about 911 Communications in Neosho County.\nAppraiser\nAccess more information about the Neosho County Appraiser and services available.\nClerk\nFind more information about the Clerk's Office.\nCounty Attorney\nBrowse important Attorney information for Neosho County.\nElections\nBrowse election information in Neosho County.\nEmergency Management\nBrowse information provided by the Emergency Management Department.\nGIS / Floodplain\nGeographic Information Systems (GIS) is a set of tools for the collection and maintenance of databases and their spatial position. These tools are capable of creating maps and figures to display a multitude of data and the geographic position of that data within a particular area.\nHealth Department\nThe mission of the Neosho County Health Department (NCHD) is to provide a wide range of health services that have a demonstrated need in the community, giving priority to those services which are not or cannot be provided at an affordable rate by other sectors of the community.\nHuman Resources\nNoxious Weed\nContact the Noxious Weeds Department.\nRegister of Deeds\nThe Register of Deeds is an elected official who is required by the Laws of the State of Kansas to record all documents submitted by the public which are qualified to be recorded; maintain an up-to-date and accurate set of indexes that show the correct ownership of land in the entire county and perform all functions of a clerical and technical nature to accomplish that objective.\nRoad & Bridge / Landfill\nFind contact information for Road and Bridge/Landfill.\nSanitation LEPP\nReview more information about Sanitation LEPP.\nSheriff\nLearn more about the Sheriff's office in Neosho County.\nTreasurer\nReview important information from the Treasurer's office.\nContact Us\nNeosho County Courthouse\n100 South Main Street\nErie, KS 66733\nPhone : 620-244-3800\nQuick Links\n31st Judicial Center\nNeosho County Community College\nNeosho County Extension\nNeosho County Hospital\nUSD 413 Public Schools\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nHelpful Links\nHome\nSite Map\nContact Us\nAccessibility\nCopyright Notices\nPrivacy Policy\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nGovernment Websites by CivicPlus®\nLoading\nLoading\nDo Not Show Again\nClose\nPageAssist\nDiscover your personalization options\nClose ×",
